---
// Two teams and one interface: both design to the ICD, never to the other team's current model.
const ink = 'var(--rd-ink)', muted = 'var(--rd-muted)', accent = 'var(--rd-accent)', blue = 'var(--rd-blue)', ok = 'var(--rd-ok)';
const fields = ['Geometry and datums', 'Tolerance split', 'Loads, both directions', 'Temperatures', 'Sealing: groove and face', 'Fasteners and torque', 'Bonding and earthing', 'Freeze date'];
---

<figure class="viz icdboundary">
  <p class="viz-title">Both sides design to the ICD</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 360 244" role="img" aria-labelledby="icdboundary-desc" style="max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <desc id="icdboundary-desc">
      The motor team on the left and the nozzle supplier on the right each design their part to the interface control
      document in the middle. The ICD defines the geometry and datums, the tolerance split, the loads in both
      directions, the temperatures, which side has the seal groove and which the face, the fasteners and torque, the
      electrical bonding, and the freeze date. A crossed-out dashed line between the two teams shows that neither
      designs to the other team's current model.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="icd-arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="context-stroke"></path></marker>
    </defs>
    <rect x="8" y="70" width="80" height="64" rx="6" fill={blue} fill-opacity="0.18" stroke={blue}></rect>
    <text x="48" y="98" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ink}>Motor team</text>
    <text x="48" y="113" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill={muted}>closure</text>
    <rect x="272" y="70" width="80" height="64" rx="6" fill={ok} fill-opacity="0.18" stroke={ok}></rect>
    <text x="312" y="98" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ink}>Nozzle team</text>
    <text x="312" y="113" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill={muted}>nozzle</text>
    <rect x="100" y="12" width="160" height="180" rx="6" fill="var(--rd-panel)" stroke={ink}></rect>
    <text x="180" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill={ink}>ICD</text>
    {fields.map((t, k) => <text x="108" y={50 + k * 18} font-size="9" fill={ink}>{t}</text>)}
    <line x1="88" x2="98" y1="102" y2="102" stroke={blue} stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#icd-arr)"></line>
    <line x1="272" x2="262" y1="102" y2="102" stroke={ok} stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#icd-arr)"></line>
    <path d="M48,134 Q48,214 180,214 Q312,214 312,134" fill="none" stroke={accent} stroke-dasharray="4 3"></path>
    <line x1="172" x2="188" y1="206" y2="222" stroke={accent} stroke-width="2"></line>
    <line x1="188" x2="172" y1="206" y2="222" stroke={accent} stroke-width="2"></line>
    <text x="180" y="238" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9.5" fill={accent}>not to the other team's CAD</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Interfaces fail at the boundary between teams, not between parts. The ICD is the only document that both teams can
    be held to. Each change goes through it, with both signatures.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
